.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1000 AM PST Wed Nov 18 2026

Frontal boundary passing over SFO at this time with a wind shift
to westerly already noted at San Francisco buoy located west of
the Golden Gate. Very strong SE wind gusts continue in the warm
sector with San Jose gusting 44 kt last observation. Boundary will
continue to shift south through today with steady rain turning
more showery later this afternoon and evening. With parent upper
low still well to our NW the surface winds will maintain a S/SE
wind direction (perhaps slight backing during frontal passage).

Vicinity of SFO...Frontal boundary passing over airport near 18z
with pressure rising and brief wind shift to more southerly vs SE,
however winds will maintain southerly component til Thursday
morning given location of upper low. Periods of rain with low cigs
to continue today into Thursday morning.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO with visuals impacted and
southerly winds.

Monterey Bay Terminals...SE winds ahead of front to continue
through the afternoon hours with heaviest rains arriving closer to
00z. SE winds switch more SW overnight into early Thursday
morning.

