.MARINE...
(Tonight through next Monday)
Issued at 145 PM PST Wed Nov 18 2026

A cold front from a strong low pressure system will sweep across
the  coastal waters and bays today, bringing moderate to heavy
rain and strong winds. Winds will decrease from north to south to
a moderate to fresh breeze behind the cold front later today and
tonight. A few storm force gusts may occur with frontal passage.
The low will then follow through, bringing more showers and
thunderstorms tonight  into Thursday. Expect hazardous marine
conditions over the course  of this system including widespread
gales, moderate to heavy rain, and a slight chance of
thunderstorms. Another cold front will  bring rain and gusty winds
later Saturday into early Sunday.

